{title: Come Thou Fount}
{artist: Robert Robinson}
{key: D}
{youtube: https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Come+Thou+Fount+hymn}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Come thou [A]Fount of [Bm]every [G]blessing
[D]Tune my [A]heart to [G]sing thy [D]grace
[D]Streams of [A]mercy, [Bm]never [G]ceasing
[D]Call for [A]songs of [G]loudest [D]praise
[D]Teach me [A]some me[Bm]lodious [G]sonnet
[D]Sung by [A]flaming [G]tongues a[D]bove
[D]Praise the [A]mount, I'm [Bm]fixed up[G]on it
[D]Mount of [A]Thy re[G]deeming [D]love
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Come thou [D]Fount of [A]every [D]blessing
[G]Tune my [D]heart to [A]sing thy [D]grace
{end_of_chorus}
